---
import StaticPageLayout from "../layouts/StaticPageLayout.astro";
---

<StaticPageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="PRIVACY"
  description="How LUDIVON approaches privacy and the information that may be processed when the publication becomes publicly available."
>
  <div class="prelaunch-note">
    <p>
      <strong>Pre-launch notice:</strong>
      This is an initial privacy notice for the development
      version of LUDIVON. It is not the final public privacy
      policy. It must be reviewed and completed against the
      actual hosting, analytics and advertising configuration
      before public launch.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>1. About this notice</h2>

  <p>
    LUDIVON is an independent gaming and technology publication
    from TGG HUB.
  </p>

  <p>
    This notice explains the current privacy-related design
    of the publication and identifies matters that must be
    finalised before its public launch.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Current website functionality</h2>

  <p>
    The current development implementation is a static
    publication website.
  </p>

  <p>
    It does not currently provide:
  </p>

  <ul class="policy-list">
    <li>Reader accounts or user profiles.</li>
    <li>Comments or public discussion features.</li>
    <li>Newsletter registration or subscription infrastructure.</li>
    <li>Reader payment or checkout functionality.</li>
    <li>Reader-facing advertising management features.</li>
    <li>A website contact or enquiry submission form.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    No third-party advertising network or analytics script
    has been integrated into the current website source.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Technical information</h2>

  <p>
    When a website is hosted and accessed, its hosting and
    delivery providers may process technical request information
    for purposes such as delivering pages, maintaining security,
    diagnosing errors and preventing abuse.
  </p>

  <p>
    Depending on the actual provider and configuration, this
    may include information such as an IP address, browser
    or device information, requested resources and request
    timestamps.
  </p>

  <p>
    The final policy will identify the actual hosting provider,
    relevant processing purposes and applicable retention
    information once the production configuration is established.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>

  <p>
    No advertising or analytics technology is currently
    integrated into the website source.
  </p>

  <p>
    Any future cookies, local storage, tracking technologies
    or consent mechanisms will be reviewed against the actual
    services being introduced and applicable requirements.
    The policy will be updated before those technologies
    are activated.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Advertising and third-party services</h2>

  <p>
    Advertising is the planned revenue model for LUDIVON,
    but advertising is not active in the current implementation.
  </p>

  <p>
    Before any advertising network or analytics service is
    activated, the privacy implications, relevant third parties,
    data collected and applicable consent requirements must
    be reviewed and documented.
  </p>

  <p>
    External websites linked from LUDIVON operate under
    their own privacy practices.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Contact and enquiries</h2>

  <p>
    The current development website does not include a contact
    form or reader account system.
  </p>

  <p>
    A verified privacy and general contact route will be
    published before public launch so readers can direct
    appropriate privacy-related enquiries to the publisher.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Data retention and security</h2>

  <p>
    Any information processed by future hosting, security,
    analytics or advertising providers will be subject to
    the actual service configuration and applicable retention
    practices.
  </p>

  <p>
    The final policy will describe relevant retention periods
    and safeguards after those arrangements have been confirmed.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Privacy requests</h2>

  <p>
    The final public policy will explain the applicable
    privacy rights, how requests can be submitted and how
    they will be handled.
  </p>

  <p>
    Those details must be completed using the actual legal
    operator information, applicable jurisdiction and
    production services before launch.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>

  <p>
    This notice will be revised when the actual public
    website, hosting, analytics or advertising configuration
    is finalised.
  </p>
</StaticPageLayout>